node.doctext:
I am processing data from a webservice and my code has many instances of this that processes different types of data:
<code>
my $data = $api->request(...);
for my $item ($api->collect($data)) {
    process($item);
    for my $widget ($api->gather($item->{sets}{widgets})) {
        process($widget);
    }
}
</code>
The <code>collect</code> method converts the parsed data into a list of items, and if a pagination indicator is found, 
it makes another api request, parses the data and adds it to the accumulator, ..., until no pagination indicator is found, then returns the accumulated items.
<p>
This is not a good design, since the memory usage can rise unacceptably high, so I'd like to change the implementation details of <code>collect</code> to make use of an iterator or tied array and avoid accumulating, but I would also like to keep the current user interface of simply iteratoring over the results with a for loop. Is this possible?
